    <script type="application/ld+json">
      {"@context":"http://schema.org","@graph":[{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"DiscussionForumPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"ORS Consulting (ORS)","url":"https://no.linkedin.com/company/orsconsulting"},"datePublished":"2026-09-04T08:15:02.686Z","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/orsconsulting_saf-sustainableaviationfutures-energytransition-activity-7501553400547917824-92uB","text":"Next week, the ORS Consulting team will be at the Sustainable Aviation Futures (SAF) Congress Garden Party in London, and we're excited to be sponsoring the event.\n\nThe SAF industry continues to gain momentum, with ambitious projects being developed across the UK and internationally. We are proud to support organisations in delivering these projects safely through our expertise in industrial risk management.\n\nMeet our colleagues Neill Renton, Samuel Richardson and Morten Nilstad Pettersen on the 10th of September. We look forward to catching up with existing contacts, making new connections and learning more about the exciting developments taking place across the SAF landscape.\n\nThe event is now fully booked but the wait list is open. If you'll be there, feel free to reach out and say hello.\n\n#SAF #SustainableAviationFutures #EnergyTransition #ProcessSafety #IndustrialRisk","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/orsconsulting_saf-sustainableaviationfutures-energytransition-activity-7501553400547917824-92uB"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"DiscussionForumPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"ORS Consulting (ORS)","url":"https://no.linkedin.com/company/orsconsulting"},"datePublished":"2026-09-02T07:43:41.923Z","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/orsconsulting_process-qra-vs-explosives-qra-understanding-activity-7500820735863578625-QsKW","text":"What distinguishes an Explosives QRA from a Process QRA?\n\nIn this insight, Hampus Henriksson explores the key differences between Process QRA and Explosives QRA, explaining why facilities handling energetic materials (such as explosives, propellants, ammunition, etc.) require specialised approaches to hazard identification, frequency modelling, and consequence assessment.\n\nRead more 👉 https://lnkd.in/dN9P7c5J","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/orsconsulting_process-qra-vs-explosives-qra-understanding-activity-7500820735863578625-QsKW"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"DiscussionForumPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"ORS Consulting (ORS)","url":"https://no.linkedin.com/company/orsconsulting"},"datePublished":"2026-08-19T10:26:00.345Z","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/orsconsulting_we-are-grateful-to-be-part-of-the-oeuk-community-activity-7495788151693791232-2GsD","text":"We are grateful to be part of the OEUK community!\n\nThank you Offshore Energies UK 👏 ","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/orsconsulting_we-are-grateful-to-be-part-of-the-oeuk-community-activity-7495788151693791232-2GsD"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"DiscussionForumPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"ORS Consulting (ORS)","url":"https://no.linkedin.com/company/orsconsulting"},"datePublished":"2026-07-02T07:04:03.669Z","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/orsconsulting_understanding-dsear-and-atex-managing-fire-activity-7478342713084416000-kkj9","text":"Understanding DSEAR and ATEX: More than a Compliance Requirement\n\nManaging fire and explosion risks is a fundamental responsibility for organisations operating in environments where flammable substances are present.\n\nWhile DSEAR and ATEX are well-established frameworks, many businesses continue to face challenges in understanding how the requirements interact and how they should be applied throughout the lifecycle of a facility.\n\nA robust approach to hazardous area classification, equipment selection, and risk management not only supports regulatory compliance but also contributes to safer operations, reduced operational risk, and improved asset integrity.\n\nIn this article, Alessandro Capaldi provides an overview of the key principles behind DSEAR and ATEX, and important considerations for organisations seeking to effectively manage fire and explosion hazards.\n\n📖 Read the full article here: https://lnkd.in/dJ7_Vr66\n\n#ProcessSafety #ATEX #DSEAR #ExplosionProtection #RiskManagement #SafetyEngineering #ORSConsulting","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/orsconsulting_understanding-dsear-and-atex-managing-fire-activity-7478342713084416000-kkj9"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"DiscussionForumPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"ORS Consulting (ORS)","url":"https://no.linkedin.com/company/orsconsulting"},"datePublished":"2026-05-26T07:30:11.161Z","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/orsconsulting_simops-qra-processsafety-activity-7464940936620306432-qThT","text":"How can QRA be used for assessing risks arising from SIMOPS?\n\nSpecial operations such as construction, decommissioning and drilling are often performed next to process plants in operation. These Simultaneous Operations (SIMOPS) introduce new hazards: more people in the hazard zone, new ignition sources, and an increased risk of loss of containment (e.g., from dropped objects).\n\nIn our latest insight, Carsten Stegelmann explains how a SIMOPS QRA differs from a traditional design QRA and how it can support better decisions and demonstrate ALARP.\n\nRead more: https://lnkd.in/dBJveiJc\n\n#SIMOPS #QRA #ProcessSafety #TechnicalSafety #RiskManagement #ORSConsulting","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/orsconsulting_simops-qra-processsafety-activity-7464940936620306432-qThT"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"DiscussionForumPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"ORS Consulting (ORS)","url":"https://no.linkedin.com/company/orsconsulting"},"datePublished":"2026-04-28T11:40:44.555Z","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/orsconsulting_from-compliance-to-value-functional-safety-activity-7454857130995732481-Ralh","text":"How can structured functional safety unlock synergies in GMP application?\n\nIn this insight Lisa Josan explores how functional safety can support safer operations, improved reliability, and clearer decision-making throughout the lifecycle of pharmaceutical facilities. It also highlights how functional safety work aligns well with GMP requirements, supporting documentation, traceability, validation, and change control, and how pharmaceutical companies can benefit from synergies between safety and quality frameworks rather than managing them in isolation.\n\nRead more 👉  https://lnkd.in/gzCNpfc3","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/orsconsulting_from-compliance-to-value-functional-safety-activity-7454857130995732481-Ralh"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"DiscussionForumPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"ORS Consulting (ORS)","url":"https://no.linkedin.com/company/orsconsulting"},"datePublished":"2026-04-15T08:09:38.677Z","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/orsconsulting_with-nis2-now-in-force-many-operators-are-activity-7450092964216938496-XMft","text":"With NIS2 now in force, many operators are assessing what a cyber security risk assessment actually means in an OT context. The challenge is rarely the requirement itself, but to integrate the cyber security work with other areas within risk management. Operations teams may be left out of the conversation, and the link to process consequences and SIS documentation can be lost. Without integration and alignment with other disciplines, the result is a report that satisfies a checkbox without providing much value. \n \nIn our experience, effective CSRAs in industrial environments benefit from a cross-disciplinary approach from the start: \n• Integration with existing PHA studies (HAZOP/LOPA)\n• Involvement from operations and engineering disciplines \n• Structured methodology grounded in IEC 62443 and aligned with IEC 61511.\n \nThe output should give operators a clearer picture of how cyber events can propagate into process consequences, and whether existing safeguards are adequate. This requires understanding the process, the control system, and the safety functions. \n \nRead more about integrating cyber security in process safety management here: https://lnkd.in/emGAdJJ3","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/orsconsulting_with-nis2-now-in-force-many-operators-are-activity-7450092964216938496-XMft"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"DiscussionForumPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"ORS Consulting (ORS)","url":"https://no.linkedin.com/company/orsconsulting"},"datePublished":"2026-03-31T11:50:47.848Z","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/orsconsulting_bridging-academia-and-industry-last-friday-activity-7444712801144614912-r6RZ","text":"Bridging academia and industry - Last Friday our colleague Per Ståle Larsen gave a guest lecture at NTNU in Trondheim.\n\nThe lecture provided the students with insights on how risk analysis methods are used in the industry and why understanding the context is key. In addition, real life examples of risk analysis application were presented.\n\nThank you Nicola Paltrinieri for organising the lecture and to all students who attended!","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/orsconsulting_bridging-academia-and-industry-last-friday-activity-7444712801144614912-r6RZ"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"DiscussionForumPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"ORS Consulting (ORS)","url":"https://no.linkedin.com/company/orsconsulting"},"datePublished":"2026-03-26T08:30:07.905Z","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/orsconsulting_wehra-workingenvironment-hse-activity-7442850362681802752-czdN","text":"What is WEHRA (Working Environment Health Risk Assessment)? \n\nIn our latest insight, I. Caroline Vaaland Holmgard explains the WEHRA method, its purpose, and key advantages. \n\nWEHRA is one structured approach for assessing and managing health risks related to both existing and future workplaces in design. The method addresses key working environment factors, including ergonomics, noise and vibration, chemicals, radiation, human factors, psychosocial conditions, outdoor operations, and biological hazards.\n \nA structured WEHRA approach helps manage health risks by:\n\n• People‑ and task‑centred assessment of normal operation and maintenance activities\n• Interdisciplinary workshops with active end‑user involvement\n• Early risk identification and cross‑disciplinary alignment avoiding late design changes\n• Supporting informed decisions throughout the workplace lifecycle\n \n👉 Read more about the WEHRA: https://lnkd.in/gnkKeJh2\n\n#WEHRA #WorkingEnvironment #HSE #RiskAssessment #Operations #HumanFactors #Engineering","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/orsconsulting_wehra-workingenvironment-hse-activity-7442850362681802752-czdN"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"DiscussionForumPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"ORS Consulting (ORS)","url":"https://no.linkedin.com/company/orsconsulting"},"datePublished":"2026-03-17T08:56:44.260Z","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/orsconsulting_fera-technicalsafety-riskmanagement-activity-7439595567426572288-tQti","text":"The importance of conducting a FERA\n \nFire and Explosion Risk Assessment (FERA) is critical for process facilities handling flammable materials posing a fire or explosion risk. \n\nIn this insight, Carsten Stegelmann explains:\n • The key advantages of conducting a FERA and why it is important \n • The FERA methodology \n • How FERA relates to other safety deliverables\n • Management of assumptions and uncertainties\n \n👉 Read the article here: https://lnkd.in/esyCszmb\n\n#FERA #TechnicalSafety #RiskManagement #ORSConsulting","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/orsconsulting_fera-technicalsafety-riskmanagement-activity-7439595567426572288-tQti"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"Organization","name":"ORS Consulting (ORS)","url":"https://no.linkedin.com/company/orsconsulting","address":{"type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":"Lilleakerveien 4a","addressLocality":"Oslo","postalCode":"0283","addressCountry":"NO"},"description":"ORS Consulting was established in 2009 with an aim to provide to-the-point consultancy services. The company built its reputation as risk and safety consultants for the offshore oil and gas industry, which is exposed to major accident risks due to the harsh environment, aging installations and expanding subsea and deep-water operations. \n\nToday, ORS Consulting provides technical risk management and process engineering advisory services supporting multiple industries, including green energy transition industries, chemicals, oil and gas, power and utilities, aquaculture and maritime. ORS is an employee-owned company with offices and businesses in Sweden, Norway, Denmark, Türkiye and the United Kingdom. \n \nThe corner stone of our business strategy is to focus on \"to-the-point\" and meaningful advisory. Our clients appreciate the way ORS combines the specialist skills with a pragmatic- and cooperative approach.","numberOfEmployees":{"value":80,"@type":"QuantitativeValue"},"logo":{"contentUrl":"https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D4D0BAQF8wMDeAJRwbg/company-logo_200_200/company-logo_200_200/0/1738842202595/orsconsulting_logo?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=3g9q1oS7xV4DaWNE_czziwWcd20PBbmFgr4P-3QeAG0","description":"ORS Consulting (ORS)","@type":"ImageObject"},"slogan":"ORS is a specialist provider of industrial risk management and process engineering advisory services.","sameAs":"https://www.ors-consulting.com/"}]}
    </script>
  
  
      
