    <p class="attributed-text-segment-list__content text-color-text !text-sm whitespace-pre-wrap break-words
        " dir="ltr" data-test-id="main-feed-activity-card__commentary">What distinguishes an Explosives QRA from a Process QRA?

In this insight, <a class="link" href="https://se.linkedin.com/in/hampus-henriksson-666b62239?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Hampus Henriksson</a> explores the key differences between Process QRA and Explosives QRA, explaining why facilities handling energetic materials (such as explosives, propellants, ammunition, etc.) require specialised approaches to hazard identification, frequency modelling, and consequence assessment.

Read more 👉 <a class="link" href="https://lnkd.in/dN9P7c5J?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/dN9P7c5J</a></p>
