  <div class="attributed-text-segment-list__container relative mt-1 mb-1.5 babybear:mt-0 babybear:mb-0.5">
    <p class="attributed-text-segment-list__content text-color-text !text-sm whitespace-pre-wrap break-words
        " dir="ltr" data-test-id="main-feed-activity-card__commentary">How can structured functional safety unlock synergies in GMP application?

In this insight <a class="link" href="https://dk.linkedin.com/in/lisa-josan-a967b714b?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Lisa Josan</a> explores how functional safety can support safer operations, improved reliability, and clearer decision-making throughout the lifecycle of pharmaceutical facilities. It also highlights how functional safety work aligns well with GMP requirements, supporting documentation, traceability, validation, and change control, and how pharmaceutical companies can benefit from synergies between safety and quality frameworks rather than managing them in isolation.

Read more 👉  <a class="link" href="https://lnkd.in/gzCNpfc3?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/gzCNpfc3</a></p>
